---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import Section from '../components/Section.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro'
---
<Base title={'Ommisa CLI'} description={'The Ommisa CLI runs the same assistant at the terminal: a thread that holds context, piped input, images on a question, machine-readable output, and a local log.'}>
<div class="page-narrow prose">
  <Hero title="Ommisa CLI" lede="The command-line interface runs the same assistant at the terminal. The reply is the only text written to standard output, while the progress indicator, the citations and the warnings ride standard error, so that redirection and pipes stay clean.">
  </Hero>

  <Section id="install" title="Installation">
    <CodeBlock title="requires Node.js 18+" code={`npm install -g @ommisa/cli
ommisa status`} />
    <p>The package carries no runtime dependencies. <code>ommisa status</code> reports the service, the signed-in account, and where the day's quota stands.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="signin" title="Signing in">
    <CodeBlock title="device flow — approve the code in the browser" code={`ommisa login
ommisa login --read-only
ommisa whoami
ommisa logout`} />
    <p>Sign-in runs the device authorization flow, which presents a code for approval in the browser and stores credentials under <code>~/.config/ommisa/credentials.json</code> with mode 0600. The default scope grants read and write access, the <code>--read-only</code> option drops the write scope, and a read-only sign-in refuses the storage of conversations and memory files. Without credentials, every command uses the public tier.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="asking" title="Asking questions">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa ask "What is the MPE requirement for a load cell per OIML R 60?"
ommisa ask --lang fr "Qu'est-ce que l'EMT d'une cellule de charge ?"
ommisa ask "..." --attach nameplate.png
cat report.md | ommisa ask "Summarize this against R 60."
ommisa ask "..." --save
ommisa ask -c "..."`} />
    <p>The tier, the remaining quota and the sign-in instruction print with every answer. The <code>--fresh</code> option bypasses the answer caches, the <code>--save</code> option stores the question and its answer as a conversation, the <code>--conversation &lt;id&gt;</code> option continues a stored conversation, and the <code>-c</code> option continues the most recent one. The <code>--attach</code> option places a PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF image of at most 4 MB on the question, and a photograph is examined only with the question it accompanies. Piped standard input becomes the question's context.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="chat" title="A thread in the terminal">
    <CodeBlock title="ommisa chat" code={`› What is the MPE for a class III load cell?
› and for class IIII?
/new      clears the thread
/attach FILE   puts an image on the next question
/lang fr answers in French from here on
/save     stores the thread to your account
/exit`} />
    <p>Every follow-up question rides the thread's history, and answers written in Markdown render for the terminal when standard output is a screen.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="composing" title="Composing with other tools">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa ask "..." --json         # the full response document on stdout
ommisa ask "..." --stream-json  # NDJSON events: stage, token, done
ommisa ask "..." -o answer.md   # the markdown reply to a file
ommisa log [N]                  # the last asks from this machine's log`} />
    <p>The <code>--json</code> option prints the machine-readable response, which carries the answer, its citations, the measured confidence, the entailment support and the quota. The exit code is a contract, in which <strong>0</strong> reports a delivered answer, <strong>1</strong> reports a failure, <strong>2</strong> reports a usage error, <strong>4</strong> reports a spent quota and <strong>130</strong> reports an interruption.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="memory" title="Memory files, conversations and projects">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa memories
ommisa memories add "Our lab" "We verify load cells to R 60."
ommisa conversations
ommisa conversations show <id>
ommisa files [project-id]`} />
    <p>Selected memory files join each question as context. Conversations store threads across machines, and projects bind conversations and files into one context in the web application.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="config" title="Configuration">
    <p>The environment variables <code>OMMISA_ID</code>, <code>OMMISA_API</code>, <code>OMMISA_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>OMMISA_SCOPE</code> override the defaults, and each also takes a command-line flag. Every question lands in the local log at <code>~/.config/ommisa/log.jsonl</code>, and the log never leaves the machine.</p>
  </Section>
</div>
</Base>
